# Replication package


The package goes from the raw data to every table and figure of the paper and of its Online Appendix, in three steps, all run from the `replication/` folder:

| Step | Command | Time | Output |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1. Build the panels from the raw data (optional) | `Rscript code/construction/00_build_panel.R` | under 1 min | Rebuilds the two analysis panels in `replication/rebuild/` and checks them against `data/processed/` (`results/check_panel_rebuild.txt`) |
| 2. All new or revised tables and figures | `Rscript code/00_run_all.R` | about 2 min | `tables/`, `figures/`, `replication/results/`, `replication/logs/` |
| 3. Figures unchanged since the submitted version (Figures 1, 3, 5) | `Rscript code/unchanged_figures/00_run_unchanged_figures.R` | under 1 min | `replication/output/` |

Step 2 uses the processed panels shipped in `data/processed/`, so it can be run without step 1. In our checks, step 1 reproduces both panels exactly (every column, every observation), and step 2 reproduces every table of the manuscript to the last digit. The manuscript is then compiled from the root folder (Section 6).

## 2. Data

All raw files are in `replication/data/raw/`.

| File | Source | Used for |
|---|---|---|
| `WEOOct2023all.csv` | IMF World Economic Outlook, October 2023 | Debt, primary balance, revenue, expenditure, growth, inflation, current account |
| `GPR_historical_data.xls` | Caldara and Iacoviello (2022), monthly global and country indices (vintage used in the paper) | GPR shock |
| `data_gpr_export_2026-11-04.xls` | Same source, downloaded on 4 November 2026 | Vintage check (identical over 1990–2022) |
| `FRD_dataset.xlsx` | IMF Fiscal Rules Dataset (Davoodi et al., 2022) | Fiscal rules, escape clauses, fiscal councils |
| `GSDB_v3.csv` | Global Sanctions Data Base, version 3 (Felbermayr et al., 2020) | Sanctions by type |
| `datawar.xlsx` | UCDP/PRIO Armed Conflict Dataset, country-year extract | Armed-conflict indicators |
| `Global_Policy_Uncertainty_Data.xlsx` | Baker, Bloom and Davis (2016), global EPU index (policyuncertainty.com; series GEPU_ppp, also distributed by FRED as GEPUPPP) | EPU shock |
| `wdi_demographics.csv` | World Bank World Development Indicators, downloaded with the WDI R package | Five demographic variables kept in the panel; not used in the estimations |

Data access: all sources are public. The Global Sanctions Data Base is distributed by its authors on request for research use; users should cite it and check its terms before redistributing the file. `code/construction/c07_demographics_download.R` downloads the WDI series again (internet access and the `WDI` and `countrycode` packages are needed); `c07_demographics.R` reads the stored copy.

Processed data (`replication/data/processed/`):

- `panel_analytique_FINAL_v3.rds`: panel of 60 emerging and developing economies, 1990–2022 (1,980 country-years, 87 variables).
- `panel_frd_extended.rds`: the same panel with the fiscal-council and escape-clause variables (102 variables).
- `gpr_country_annual.csv`: annual country GPR index and AR(1) shock for the 19 countries with a country-specific index, built by `code/00_gpr_country.R`.

## 3. Software

R 4.3.3. Packages: `data.table` (1.14.10), `ggplot2` (3.4.4), `brglm2` (0.9.2), `sandwich` (3.1.0), `readxl` (1.4.3) for steps 2 and 3; in addition `tidyverse`, `writexl`, `janitor` and `patchwork` for steps 1 and 3. The construction scripts must run in a UTF-8 locale, because some WEO country names are accented; the master scripts set it. The estimators (two-way fixed-effects local projections, standard errors clustered by country, Driscoll–Kraay standard errors, wild cluster bootstrap, probit and Firth average marginal effects) are coded in the scripts; `fixest` and `margins` are not required. `code/01_check_vs_fixest.R` shows that the local-projection code reproduces `fixest` output to three decimals (run it with `GPR_MEASURE=submitted`, the measure for which the reference values were recorded). LaTeX (pdflatex, bibtex) and the package `xr-hyper` are needed to compile the manuscript.

Random seeds: wild cluster bootstrap 20261027; country-block bootstrap of Online Appendix Table OA.2: 1.

